        "type": "note",
        "content": "Senior Engineer Insight: Never use Optional for class fields or method parameters. Doing so creates unnecessary heap pressure and forces the caller to wrap values in Optional objects, violating the principle of least astonishment. If you find yourself writing 'if (opt.isPresent()) { get() }', you are likely misusing the API; refactor to use functional operators like map() or filter() to keep your code declarative."
