        "type": "prose",
        "content": "In the context of the Java Stream API, these four operations represent the core functional transformations used to process collections. 'map' is a one-to-one transformation; it applies a function to each element, producing exactly one output element per input element, effectively changing the type or value of the stream. 'flatMap' is a one-to-many transformation; it maps each element to a stream of values and then flattens those streams into a single, continuous stream, which is critical for handling nested structures like List<List<T>>. 'filter' acts as a predicate-based gatekeeper, retaining only elements that satisfy a boolean condition, thereby reducing the stream size. 'peek' is a non-interfering, stateful-debug operation that allows you to perform an action (like logging) on each element as it is consumed, without modifying the stream's structure or flow."
