      {
        "type": "code",
        "language": "java",
        "content": "@Service\npublic class OrderService {\n    // Use CompletableFuture for non-blocking I/O to handle high concurrency\n    public CompletableFuture<OrderResponse> processOrderAsync(OrderRequest request) {\n        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> {\n            // Offload to thread pool to avoid blocking the main request thread\n            return orderRepository.save(request);\n        }, customExecutor);\n    }\n}"
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "content": "The most common trap for engineers scaling to 1M users is 'premature database optimization.' Before implementing complex sharding or NoSQL migration, ensure your query execution plans are optimal and that you have proper indexing. A single missing index on a table with 10 million rows will kill your system faster than any lack of microservices architecture ever could. Always profile before you scale."
      }
