        "type": "prose",
        "content": "The most challenging backend problem I encountered involved a non-deterministic 'Stop-the-World' latency spike in a high-throughput trading engine. We were dealing with a massive object graph in the JVM heap that triggered frequent Full Garbage Collection cycles. The root cause was a combination of 'Memory Fragmentation' and 'Object Allocation Rate' exceeding the capacity of the Young Generation, causing premature promotion of short-lived objects to the Old Generation. This resulted in 'Tenured Space' saturation and cascading GC pauses that stalled our order matching logic, leading to significant slippage in trade execution."
