      {
        "type": "code",
        "language": "java",
        "content": "public class BufferPool {\n    private final Queue<ByteBuffer> pool = new ConcurrentLinkedQueue<>();\n    \n    public ByteBuffer acquire() {\n        ByteBuffer buffer = pool.poll();\n        return (buffer != null) ? buffer : ByteBuffer.allocateDirect(1024);\n    }\n\n    public void release(ByteBuffer buffer) {\n        buffer.clear();\n        pool.offer(buffer);\n    }\n}"
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "content": "Senior Insight: Never trust the default JVM ergonomics for latency-sensitive applications. If you see 'Promotion Failed' in your GC logs, you are not just facing a memory issue; you are facing a design flaw where your object lifecycle is mismatched with your heap configuration. Always prioritize object reuse over object creation in the hot path."
      }
